{
  "abstract": "There is a countable group G such that the Bernoulli shifts of G with bases (L, lambda) and (L', lambda') are isomorphic for all standard probability spaces whose measures are not point masses: there is an equivariant, measure-preserving bijection, measurable in both directions, between shift-invariant measurable sets of full measure. No condition is put on the entropies of the bases, which may differ and may be infinite. The group is N x (Z/2 wr Z), where N is the group of the pinned OpenAI construction, which supplies the algebraic existence input. This formalization does not certify finitary or continuous conjugacy and says nothing about other groups.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Peter Burton"
    }
  ],
